# next is pinned to 15.4.11 — as high as @cloudflare/next-on-pages@1.13.16
# (the latest release, as of 2026-08-20) can go. Bisected directly
# against the real pages:build pipeline: 15.2.8 through 15.4.11 all
# build cleanly; 15.5.0 breaks immediately ("The following routes were
# not configured to run with the Edge Runtime: /_not-found") and every
# 15.5.x/15.6.x version tried after that (15.5.2, 15.5.15) fails the
# same way — the ceiling is the 15.4->15.5 boundary itself, not a
# specific declared peer range (next-on-pages claims support up to
# 15.5.2, which is also broken in practice).
#
# This already fixed the CRITICAL CVE (CVE-2025-55182, pre-auth RCE via
# React Server Components request deserialization — fixed at 15.2.6+)
# and one more HIGH (GHSA-mwv6-3258-q52c, fixed at 15.2.7+), both
# cleared by 15.2.8/15.2.9 en route to 15.4.11. The HIGH CVEs below all
# have fix floors at 15.5.x or later (SSRF, DoS) — none are reachable
# within the 15.4.x line, so they stay accepted, documented risks (see
# ROADMAP.md's tracked-risk entry) rather than blocking every PR.
# Re-evaluate the moment next-on-pages ships a release that supports
# 15.5.x+, or sooner if real user traffic/data volume changes the risk
# calculus.
